    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "What an array is"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "An **array** is a single named container that holds many values **in order**, one after another. Each value sits in a numbered slot, and the slot number is called its **index**. In almost every language the first index is **0**, so `marks[0]` is 72 and `marks[4]` is 58."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Now the teacher's program no longer cares how many students there are:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "const marks = [72, 85, 64, 91, 58];   // could be 5 or 5,000 values\n\nlet total = 0;\nfor (let i = 0; i < marks.length; i++) {\n  total += marks[i];\n}\nconsole.log(total / marks.length);    // 74"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "marks = [72, 85, 64, 91, 58]          # could be 5 or 5,000 values\n\ntotal = 0\nfor mark in marks:\n    total += mark\nprint(total / len(marks))             # 74.0"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "int[] marks = {72, 85, 64, 91, 58};   // could be 5 or 5,000 values\n\nint total = 0;\nfor (int i = 0; i < marks.length; i++) {\n    total += marks[i];\n}\nSystem.out.println((double) total / marks.length);   // 74.0"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "vector<int> marks = {72, 85, 64, 91, 58};   // could be 5 or 5,000 values\n\nint total = 0;\nfor (int i = 0; i < (int)marks.size(); i++) {\n    total += marks[i];\n}\ncout << (double)total / marks.size() << endl;   // 74"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Five students or five thousand, the code is the same four lines. That's the whole point."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Arrays in everyday life"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**A row of numbered lockers** — each locker holds one thing, and you find it by its number, not by searching.",
        "**An egg tray** — fixed slots, side by side, all holding the same kind of thing.",
        "**Seats in a cinema row** — seat 7 is always right next to seat 6 and seat 8.",
        "**The days of a month** — day 1, day 2, … each with its own box on the calendar."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Notice what they all share: the slots are **the same kind**, they are **next to each other**, and you reach any one of them **directly by its number**."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Why arrays are so useful: three superpowers"
    },
